      },
      "lineNbr": 902,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-27T00:49:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Or maybe we are assuming the irq remapping code is not expected to submit QI invalidations in parallel with pKVM initialization (e.g. it is only expected to do that much earlier, when initializing IRQ remapping, or much later, during suspend/resume)?\n\nBut if so, what exact problem is fixed by this patch?",
      "parentUuid": "d9036e81_66887c54",
      "revId": "70708fd66bc2a74ff1b3b5d01a9f2cff18dde5a4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
