      "writtenOn": "2025-11-27T16:26:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Looking at this patch again... Don\u0027t we have a race with the host\u0027s irq remapping code which may still modify DMAR_IQT_REG at any time (while we are initializing pKVM)?\n\nNice catch. cpus would be still accessing iommu MMIO space directly and it may modify IQT.\n\n\u003e Or maybe we are assuming the irq remapping code is not expected to submit QI invalidations in parallel with pKVM initialization (e.g. it is only expected to do that much earlier, when initializing IRQ remapping, or much later, during suspend/resume)?\n\nNow when I recollect more about it, this was an issue with our single hypercall patch I think. After enabling enable_pkvm switch, we initialize iommu but SRTP and TE only towards the end and there were performing invalidations and qi submits which pkvm could not handle as qi was not initialized in pkvm. I tested again today by removing the patch and I did not see any issues immediately.\n\n\u003e But if so, what exact problem is fixed by this patch?\n\nI think this patch would not be needed any more as we enable qi as soon as we receive SRTP(without this patch) and iommu driver will be doing invalidation only after SRTP. We still have a small time between hypercall enabling and SRTP, but I haven\u0027t seen any IRQ remapping invalidations during that time. As you mentioned, invalidations related to IRQ remap happen much earlier. Will spend some more time and verify that we are safe and then remove this patch. Thanks again for the deep look and noting this",
      "parentUuid": "0c34addf_6bcdde86",
      "revId": "70708fd66bc2a74ff1b3b5d01a9f2cff18dde5a4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0504c3f7_c83095e5",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/iommu.c",
